rect decisions quickly (decision quality), difficulty communicating ideas (cooperation), regarded as egocentric (cooperation), not willing to further education (adaptability). Strength: understands complicated technology, excellent attention skills (technical). So strong technical but poor cooperation.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility). Concerns: hot temper (cooperation), regarded as a loner (crew cooperation). So some cooperation issues.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. All have some cooperation concerns. Candidate A has leadership, but not open to new ideas. Candidate B has conscientiousness but communication issues. Candidate C has decision speed, technical, but egocentric and communication issues. Candidate D has responsibility, problem solving, but hot temper and loner.\n\nWhich is strongest overall? Possibly Candidate A: strong anticipation, leadership, technical, but health and openness issues. Candidate B: stress, conscientiousness, but communication issues. Candidate D: responsibility, problem solving, but temper.\n\nWe need to make a recommendation now, but we haven't discussed all candidates yet. However we can start with a recommendation and argue. The instruction says we should still cover all candidates before final recommendation, but we can give provisional recommendation.\n\nWe should maybe start by introducing Candidate A's strengths and concerns, and give provisional vote for A, but note need to discuss others.\n\nLet's do that."}
