eration and communication, and unknown memory impact; C strong reliability, calmness, decision speed, but poor communication, egocentric, not willing to further education; D strong problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but arrogance, know-it-all, possible cooperation issues.\n\nWe need to make an argument. Perhaps we can argue that Candidate C's reliability and calmness under crisis are critical, and despite communication issues, his egocentric nature may be mitigated by training, while A lacks evidence on stress resilience. Or we could argue that B's stress handling and conscientiousness outweigh his communication concerns, but we need to consider memory for numbers.\n\nWe need to decide a provisional vote. Considering the evidence, I think Candidate C stands out for reliability (100% reliable) and calmness in crisis, plus quick correct decisions. However, his communication difficulty and egocentric attitude could be serious for crew cooperation. But we haven't discussed his cooperation yet. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving, but arrogance.\n\nMaybe we should propose Candidate C as a strong alternative, but note concerns. Or we could still be undecided and ask for more info on C's cooperation. But we need to make a contribution with a vote. The instruction: \"Your PUBLIC_MESSAGE must: - state or clearly imply your current hiring recommendation\". So we need to vote for one candidate. We can give provisional recommendation for Candidate C, explaining why we think his strengths outweigh concerns, and note need to discuss cooperation further.\n\nAlternatively, we could keep vote for B, but we have concerns. Let's weigh: B's stress handling is proven, conscientiousness is strong reliability, but communication issues are serious for crew cooperation. C's reliability is perfect, calmness in crisis, quick decisions, but communication issues also. Which is more critical? Probably calmness under pressure and reliability are top. B's stress handling is good, but we have no evidence on decision quality under pressure. C has evidence of correct decisions quickly and calmness. So C may be stronger on safety-critical criteria. The egocentric and communication issues could be mitigated.\n\nThus I will propose Candidate C as provisional recommendation, citing his 100% reliability, calmness in crisis, quick correct decisions, but note concerns on communication and willingness to develop. I will ask for any additional evidence on his crew cooperation from other panel members later.\n\nNow craft public message: reference prior discussion: agree with Agent 2 that A lacks evidence, note B's cooperation concerns from tool answer, and propose C as strong candidate."}
