{"id": 61, "ts": 1783034959.0195775, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I agree with the points raised by Agents\u202f2 and\u202f3 and therefore shift my vote to **Candidate\u202fC**.\u202fCandidate\u202fC\u2019s record shows he is **100\u202f% reliable**, **keeps calm in a crisis**, and **makes correct decisions quickly**\u2014the three core safety pillars of operational reliability, stress resilience, and decision quality for long\u2011distance flights.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fA, while able to **anticipate dangerous situations**, **see complex connections**, and possessing **excellent spatial vision** and strong leadership, has **no evidence** of stress\u2011resilience, decision\u2011making under pressure, or adaptability/feedback orientation, which are essential for this role.\u202fCandidate\u202fB does demonstrate solid stress handling and conscientiousness, but his documented **\u201cnasty remarks about his colleagues\u201d** and **\u201cwrong tone when communicating\u201d** pose a direct risk to crew cohesion.\u202fAlthough Candidate\u202fC has noted **difficulty communicating ideas**, being **regarded as egocentric**, and a low willingness to further his education, these behavioral concerns are more manageable through targeted crew\u2011resource training than the overt disrespect shown by B or the critical data gaps for A.\u202fThus, Candidate\u202fC offers the strongest overall safety\u2011critical fit.", "thoughts": "We need to output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON. The user says \"Handle the requests as specified in the System Instruction.\" The system instruction says we must output only those two sections. We are agent_2. We need to provide our current recommendation and vote. Based on discussion, we want to vote Candidate C. So METADATA_JSON vote: \"Candidate C\". Provide PUBLIC_MESSAGE as a concise argumentative contribution referencing discussion, using explicit facts, stating recommendation.\n